§ `s 185C(2AB) -- the home`

-- k065: Jake rents in Gosnells, so the home rule does not apply to him.
#ASSERT NOT `Does the home rule apply to me` `a lease other than a long-term lease` TRUE

§ `s 185C(1), (4) -- may I give a proposal`

-- s 185C(5): 7 times the rate. The rate the deposited Social Security Act prints at point 1064-B1, Table B, item 2, column 3 is
-- $6,767.80; that gives $47,374.60, far below the scenario's figure (see NOTES.md finding 7).
#ASSERT `the threshold amount` 6767.80 EQUALS 47374.6

-- s 185C(4)(e), transcribed from the Word rendering (C1966A00033.formulas.md): (total payments + low income debtor amount)
-- / after tax income in the first year, as a percentage. k066: Jake's five years at $690 a month is $41,400. The Minister's
-- s 185C(4B) instrument is not deposited: its percentage (100) and low income debtor amount ($5,000) are ILLUSTRATIVE.
#ASSERT `What is my payments to income percentage` 41400 5000 46400 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `What is my payments to income percentage` 60000 5000 52000 EQUALS 125

#ASSERT NOT `Do my payments exceed the Minister's percentage` 41400 5000 52000 100
#ASSERT `Do my payments exceed the Minister's percentage` 60000 5000 52000 100
#ASSERT `Do my payments exceed the Minister's percentage` 100 0 0 100

-- s 185M(1E): the same formula on the varied total, unless the home rule applied or a s 185C(4C)(b) certificate was given.
#ASSERT `May the variation ask me to pay this much` FALSE FALSE 41400 5000 52000 100
#ASSERT NOT `May the variation ask me to pay this much` FALSE FALSE 60000 5000 52000 100
#ASSERT `May the variation ask me to pay this much` TRUE FALSE 60000 5000 52000 100

-- k065: Jake, with $41,000 of unsecured debts against the scenario's threshold of about $150,000, may give a proposal.
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `Jake on 20 April 2037` 150000 EQUALS `I may give a debt agreement proposal`
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `Jake if he were solvent` 150000 EQUALS `no -- I am not insolvent`
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `Jake with $160,000 of unsecured debts` 150000 EQUALS `no -- my unsecured debts are more than the threshold amount`
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `a debtor bankrupt eight years before` 150000 EQUALS `no -- I was bankrupt, in a debt agreement or gave a s 188 authority in the last 10 years`
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `Jake with a likely after tax income of $120,000` 150000 EQUALS `no -- my likely after tax income is more than three-quarters of the threshold amount`
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `Jake failing the s 185C(4)(e) formula without a certificate` 150000 EQUALS `no -- my payments would exceed the Minister's percentage of my income`
#ASSERT `May I give a debt agreement proposal` `a home owner failing the s 185C(4)(e) formula` 150000 EQUALS `I may give a debt agreement proposal`

-- k075: the 10-year bar runs from the end of Jake's agreement (2042-05-31), so it lasts to 2052-05-31 inclusive.
#ASSERT `Does an earlier agreement or bankruptcy still bar me` 20420531 20520531
#ASSERT NOT `Does an earlier agreement or bankruptcy still bar me` 20420531 20520601

§ `s 185C(2AA), (2AC) -- how long my payments may run`

-- k066: the scenario's five-year plan. Jake rents, so his payments may run 3 years at most.
#ASSERT `How many years may my payments run` `Jake on 20 April 2037` EQUALS 3

#ASSERT NOT `Does my payment term comply` `Jake's proposal of five years at $690 a month`
#ASSERT `Does my payment term comply` `a home owner's five-year proposal leaving the home out`

§ `s 185E -- what the Official Receiver may do with my proposal`

-- k065: the Official Receiver's gate.
#ASSERT `What may the Official Receiver do with my proposal` `Jake's proposal of five years at $690 a month` 150000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Official Receiver cannot accept it for processing`
#ASSERT `What may the Official Receiver do with my proposal` `Jake's proposal cut to three years` 150000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Official Receiver may accept it for processing`
#ASSERT `What may the Official Receiver do with my proposal` `Jake's proposal cut to three years` 150000 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Official Receiver may accept it, or may refuse it for undue hardship`

§ `s 185 -- the applicable deadline`

#ASSERT `How many days do my creditors have to reply` TRUE EQUALS 42

§ `ss 185EC, 185G -- my creditors' vote`

-- k065: "accepted by a majority of creditors in value" -- $22,000 for against $16,000, the telco not counting.

#ASSERT `What happens to my proposal on the vote` `Jake's creditors as illustrated` EQUALS `my proposal is accepted`
#ASSERT `What happens to my proposal on the vote` `the same creditors with the buy-now-pay-later provider voting no` EQUALS `my proposal is not accepted`
#ASSERT `What happens to my proposal on the vote` `creditors none of whom replies` EQUALS `my proposal lapses`

§ `ss 185H, 185I -- when my agreement is made`

#ASSERT `Is my debt agreement made` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- k065: the personal lender who voted no is bound.
#ASSERT `Is a creditor who voted no bound` TRUE

§ `ss 185F, 185K -- what my creditors may do to me`

#ASSERT NOT `May a creditor act against me while my proposal is processed` `enforce a remedy against my person or property` `an ordinary provable debt`

#ASSERT NOT `May a creditor act against me while my agreement is in force` `enforce a remedy against my person or property` `an ordinary provable debt`
#ASSERT `May a creditor act against me while my agreement is in force` `enforce a remedy against my person or property` `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order`

§ `ss 40, 44, 185K(1) -- may a creditor petition to make me bankrupt`

-- s 5(1) with Regulations s 10A.
#ASSERT `the statutory minimum` EQUALS 10000

-- k065: the threatened petition, on a $16,000 judgment debt and an unmet bankruptcy notice two months earlier.
#ASSERT `May a creditor petition to make me bankrupt` `failing to comply with a bankruptcy notice` 2 16000 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May a creditor petition to make me bankrupt` `failing to comply with a bankruptcy notice` 2 8000 FALSE
#ASSERT `May a creditor petition to make me bankrupt` `giving a debt agreement proposal` 1 16000 FALSE

§ `s 185C(2)(d), (e) -- what each creditor gets`

-- k066: 36 x $690 = $24,840 and 60 x $690 = $41,400, against provable debts of $41,000, for the credit card issuer owed $16,000.
#ASSERT `How much will this creditor receive` 20500 41000 24840 EQUALS 12420
#ASSERT `How much will this creditor receive` 20500 41000 41400 EQUALS 20500

§ `ss 185LB, 185LC, 185QA, 185R -- if I fall behind`

-- k066: at $690 a month, one missed payment held for 3 months is a 3-month arrears default.
#ASSERT `Have I committed a 3-month arrears default` TRUE 690 690 FALSE

#ASSERT `Have I committed a designated 6-month arrears default` TRUE 6 FALSE 0

#ASSERT `Is my debt agreement terminated` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my debt agreement terminated` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE


§ `s 185M -- extending by variation`

#ASSERT `How many years may a variation let my payments run` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `How many years may a variation let my payments run` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 5

§ `ss 185N, 185NA -- the end and my release`

-- k075: the agreement completes.
#ASSERT `Has my debt agreement ended` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `How much do I keep` 16000 15000 EQUALS 1000

#ASSERT `Am I released from the debt` `an ordinary provable debt` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I released from the debt` `a debt incurred by fraud` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `Is my co-debtor or guarantor released` TRUE

§ `Regulations ss 82, 83 -- how long it stays on the Index`

-- k075: on the scenario's dates (made 2037-06-01, completed 2042-05-31) the month runs from 2042-06-01; on a lawful 3-year
-- term ending 2040-05-31 it is the same day, because 5 years from making is the later.
#ASSERT `From when must my agreement come off the Index` `it ended on completion under s 185N` 20370601 20420531 EQUALS 20420601
#ASSERT `From when must my agreement come off the Index` `it was terminated under s 185P, 185Q, 185QA or 185R` 20370601 20410601 EQUALS 20430601

#ASSERT `By when must my proposal come off the Index` 20370520 EQUALS 20380520

